KZ3 patch 2063 (RSX pass 63): a texture read of a host zeta gets an SRV of exactly the texture's size (LD_ZWIN=0 = old).
rsx_live_draw.c: the R32F depth snapshot of a zeta is as large as the biggest pass that used its address (patch
2022). KZ3's near sun-shadow cascade (512x512 Z16 at 0x2980000 in Pyrrhus Outskirts and the other 512-cascade
levels) shares that address with the 640x360 half-resolution depth, so the snapshot is 640x512 and the sun pass,
which samples the map with normalised coordinates, looked up every receiver 1.25x too far right: sunlight indoors
(stairwell walls and ceiling lit, the overbright look). zdepth_window copies the top-left w x h of the snapshot
into a w x h R32F texture (up to 3 sizes per zeta, recopied only after the snapshot changed, CopyTextureRegion)
and binds that, so clamp-to-edge, PCF filtering, GetDimensions and unnormalised scaling see the declared texture.
Patch 2021's divide-by-snapshot-size for unnormalised zeta reads is skipped while the window is on (the window
has the texture's size). Logs: [zwin] on/off, the first 16 windows, the copy count every 16384 copies.
Upstream candidate (general: any two surfaces of different sizes at one zeta address).

